It is unlawful for any person to possess, use, consume, and/or sell any alcoholic beverage in a recreation facility owned and/or operated by Hall County, Georgia, except as may be specifically authorized by the Official Code of Hall County for professional sporting events. However, alcoholic beverage possession, use, consumption, and/or sale may be allowed in a recreation facility owned and/or operated by Hall County, Georgia for events that are approved by the Hall County Board of Commissioners (or its designee) and properly licensed or permitted by the Hall County Business License Director. In determining whether to allow the possession, use, consumption, and/or sale of alcoholic beverages within a county owned or operated recreation facility, the board of commissioners (or its designee) may consider the following factors:
(1) Whether allowing the sale or use of such beverages would violate state or local law;
(2) Whether allowing the sale or use of such beverages would violate covenants, leases, or other binding documents relating to the recreation facility at issue;
(3) Whether the proposal is appropriately limited in time and scope;
(4) Whether the proposal would adversely affect the health or safety of any person;
(5) Whether the proposal would adversely affect traffic and/or parking or create any dangerous traffic situation;
(6) Whether the proposal would adversely affect the facility or create the possibility of destruction of public property, including recreation facilities;
(7) Whether the proposal could adversely affect residents and/or businesses in the vicinity of the recreation facility at issue; or
(8) Any other factors which might rationally relate to the propriety of the request for permission to possess, use, consume, or sell alcohol in the recreation facility at issue.
(Res. of 3-12-84, § 8; Code 1991, § 2.20.140; Res. of 2-11-10(1), § 1; Res. of 4-26-12(1), § 1; Res. of 3-24-22(1), § 1)
