In addition to any and all powers enumerated in the resolutions and ordinances of the Hall County, the chairman of the board of commissioners of Hall County shall have further emergency powers as follows:
A. The chairman shall have the right to request that the Governor declare an emergency to exist when, in his opinion, one or more of the following conditions exist:
1. There is extreme likelihood of danger of destruction of life or property due to an unexpected occurrence or set of circumstances demanding immediate action;
2. Unusual or extreme weather conditions, making use of Hall County's streets or areas difficult or impossible;
3. Civil unrest, commotion, or uprising is imminent or exists; or
4. There is a stoppage or loss of electrical power affecting a major portion of Hall County's jurisdiction.
B. The declaration of an emergency as to a portion of Hall County shall specify with exactness the area in which the emergency is declared to exist.
C. After declaration of such emergency by the governor, the chairman of the board of commissioners of Hall County shall have the right to exercise any or all of the following powers:
1. The power to use Hall County employees to assist in the safety and preservation of life, limb, and property of citizenry of Hall County;
2. The power to close roads and to delineate areas within the jurisdiction of Hall County wherein an emergency exists;
3. The power to impose emergency curfew regulations;
4. The power to close business establishments within affected areas;
5. The power to close any and all governmentally owned buildings and other facilities to the use of the general public; and
6. The power to do any and all acts necessary and incident to the preservation of life, limb, and property of the citizenry of Hall County.
D. No emergency power as set forth herein shall remain in effect for more than 30 days after the declaration of an emergency by the governor and the assumption of powers by the chairman. However, upon declaration of a second or further emergencies to exist, the emergency powers as set forth herein may be extended for additional successive 30 day periods.
(Res. of 7-8-10, § 2(Exh. A); Res. of 3-24-22(2), § 2)

